course: dictionary
lesson: 8141
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-6
stars: 3
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the clues around them show you which one is meant. Representation is a good example. It can mean a picture or model that stands for something, or having someone who speaks for you.
explain: Look at the context. «Proportional representation is a different system in which a party's share of seats matches its share of votes.» Representation is not a picture here. The words «system», «seats» and «votes» are the clues, and they show it means a way of fairly sharing power.
explain: In «no taxation without representation», the colonists meant they should not have to pay taxes unless they had a say in Parliament, the body that makes the laws. Ask yourself which meaning fits the sentence, then swap it in and check that it still makes sense.
fact: Representation means showing or standing for something, or speaking for someone.
fact: A representation can be a picture, model or sign, such as a bar chart showing data.
fact: In maths, a bar model or number line is a representation of a fraction or number.
fact: «Representation» can also mean being included and shown fairly, such as «representation of girls in sport».
fact: «Taxation» means money that people pay to the government. In 1773, colonists in Boston protested against it by throwing tea into the harbour.
exercise: «Proportional representation is a different system in which a party's share of seats matches its share of votes.» What does representation mean here? | A formal complaint about the votes | *A fair system where parties get seats matching their votes | A painting of a political party leader | A sign for a political party
exercise: A maths teacher draws a bar chart to show how many children like each fruit. What kind of representation is the bar chart? | A kind of fraction | A person speaking for the class | A legal complaint | *A picture showing data
exercise: The colonists said «no taxation without representation». What did they mean? | People should pay no taxes at all | Parliament should be closed | Tea should be thrown into the harbour | *People should not be taxed unless they have a say in the lawmaking
test: Which word means a picture or model that stands for something? | taxation | harbour | election | *representation
test: When a lawyer speaks in court for you, what are they giving you? | a share of tea | a bar chart | a number line | *legal representation
exam: Read this: «Girls need fair representation in sport.» Which meaning fits best? | A picture of a sports field | A bar model for a fraction | A formal complaint to the school | *Being included and shown fairly
